triage: fix_tests: The R6 trace shows the game working as the rules say. The deck is refilled to 18 and 3 cards are dealt to each seat. A bid poll offering 0–3 stores the bids (all 0 here). Three tricks are played and resolved correctly, with seat 3 winning two and seat 2 one, and scoring applies the zero-bid +20/−20 rule. R2–R5 did not fail on what they assert (round counter, deck size, hands). They failed only on a test-side scripted rule ('option 0 offered exactly once to each seat') that the harness never matched under a 'decline' default.
